  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "MD-based evaluation of motif scaffolds and cofolding benchmarks show static predictions can overstate dynamical and conformational accuracy.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is a move away from single static structures toward dynamics and conformational ensembles as the basis for judging structural models. BILBY-PRO and BILBY-MD evaluate 220 PROSITE-derived motifs with all-atom MD and find that static refolding success overstates the dynamical fidelity of motif scaffolds. Cofolding benchmarks of AlphaFold3, RoseTTAFold3, Boltz-2 and Chai-1 on kinase and GPCR complexes report that correct ligand placement is decoupled from accurate protein conformation. ANTIOCH-VS combines ColabFold subsampling, AF2RAVE MD ensembles, docking and consensus ranking in an open-source ensemble virtual screening workflow. The PyTorch Frustratometer contributes proteome-scale local energetic frustration analysis at 70-13,000x GPU speedups with near-identical results to FrustratometeR. What is new here is the explicit dynamics-aware benchmarking of motif scaffolds; the other items contribute ensemble, frustration and cofolding analyses rather than a single shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
